Subject: Modeling Algorithms - BRepGProp_Face splits a surface of revolution's U into three spans, as a torus's
Upstream: ISSUE-TO-COME (the issue the maintainer posts on BRepGProp_Gauss's U refinement; a PR needs OCCT's CLA)
Applies to: OCCT V7_9_3.
Why: BRepGProp_Gauss::Compute with an Eps (BRepGProp::VolumeProperties(shape, props, eps),
     Silico's precise measure) never refines U: EpsU is left 0, so the U loop ends after its
     first pass, and U is integrated once over the spans BRepGProp_Face::UKnots gives. Those
     are thirds for a cylinder, cone, sphere, or torus, and one span for anything else, a
     GeomAbs_SurfaceOfRevolution included, whose U is an angle as a torus's is. So a full
     turn of an arc whose circle crosses the axis (a barrel, a dome) measured 2.2e-7 low,
     and of the fixture's two-span B-spline 3.9e-6 low, their centres of mass 9.3e-4 and
     0.033 off their axes; with three spans, whole turns to round-off (a part turn's centre
     to 2e-9). The knots are fixed at 0, 2*pi/3, 4*pi/3, as a torus's, not at the face's own
     thirds: a face whose U starts at 1 or 3 is fixed too, and one that starts past 4*pi/3
     gets a short span and a long one, up to 2.2e-7 low as before. A
     meridian of many spans keeps its residual, which is along the meridian (L), not U
     (docs/ports/measure.md). The default integration (Compute without an Eps, FreeCAD's)
     reads neither UKnots nor SUIntSubs, and is unchanged to the bit.
Moves: tests/determinism/oracle-reference.json's torus_horn summary hash, 4be84275f45be6dc
     to f3c516303caa58e7 (the horn torus is a surface of revolution; its centre of mass
     was 7.46e-6 off its origin), to be re-recorded with the maintainer. No committed
     fingerprint.
Drop when: an OCCT release's UKnots gives a surface of revolution's U spans, or when
     revolution_measures.rs and adversarial_revolution_measures.rs pass with the patch
     removed.

